      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Find the minor of ${c}_{11}$ in \n$C=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -4 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 7 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 17 & 13 & 5 & 5 \\\\ 8 & -9 & 2 & -2\\end{aligned}].$",
      "worked_solution": "To get the minor of of ${c}_{11}$, we remove the $1$st row and $1$st column:\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}3 & ∗ & ∗ & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & 7 & 0 & 1 \\\\ ∗ & 13 & 5 & 5 \\\\ ∗ & -9 & 2 & -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSo, the minor is \n\n$$\n{M}_{11}=|\\begin{aligned}7 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 13 & 5 & 5 \\\\ -9 & 2 & -2\\end{aligned}|.\n$$",
