    "q-130904": {
      "dom_id": "step-q130904",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "Find the cofactor of ${d}_{51}$ in \n$D=[\\begin{aligned}-5 & -8 & 2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 5 & 0 & 7 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 & -5 & 6 & -4 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 6 & 8 & 3 \\\\ 11 & 3 & 0 & -9 & 3\\end{aligned}].$",
      "worked_solution": "First, to get the minor of ${d}_{51}$, we remove the $5$th row and $1$st column: \n\n$$\nD=[\\begin{aligned}∗ & -8 & 2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ ∗ & 5 & 0 & 7 & 1 \\\\ ∗ & 0 & -5 & 6 & -4 \\\\ ∗ & 0 & 6 & 8 & 3 \\\\ 11 & ∗ & ∗ & ∗ & ∗\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSo, the minor is \n\n$$\n{M}_{51}=|\\begin{aligned}-8 & 2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 0 & 7 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 6 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 6 & 8 & 3\\end{aligned}|.\n$$\n\nNow, the cofactor of ${d}_{51}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{C}_{51} & =(-1)^{5+1}{M}_{51} \\\\  & ={M}_{51} \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-8 & 2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 0 & 7 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 6 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 6 & 8 & 3\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
