    "q-36043": {
      "dom_id": "step-q36043",
      "name": "Question 8",
      "problem": "Find the cofactor of ${b}_{34}$ in \n$B=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -7 & 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}].$",
      "worked_solution": "First, to get the minor of ${b}_{34}$, we remove the $3$rd row and the $4$th column: \n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 & 3 & ∗ \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0 & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗ & ∗ & -2 \\\\ -7 & 0 & 0 & ∗\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSo, the minor is \n\n$$\n{M}_{34}=|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ -7 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}|.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the cofactor of ${b}_{34}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{C}_{34} & =(-1)^{3+4}{M}_{34} \\\\  & =-{M}_{34} \\\\  & =-|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ -7 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
