    "q-32727": {
      "dom_id": "step-q32727",
      "name": "Question 11",
      "problem": "Calculate the determinant of the matrix\n$S=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -5 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 2 & 2\\end{aligned}].$",
      "worked_solution": "We use the cofactor expansion along the first row:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(S) & ={s}_{11}{C}_{11}+{s}_{12}{C}_{12}+{s}_{13}{C}_{13}+{s}_{14}{C}_{14} \\\\  & =0\\cdot {C}_{11}+2\\cdot {C}_{12}+0\\cdot {C}_{13}+0\\cdot {C}_{14} \\\\  & =2{C}_{12} \\\\  & =2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}∗ & 2 & ∗ & ∗ \\\\ 1 & ∗ & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & ∗ & -5 & 4 \\\\ 4 & ∗ & 2 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2(-1)^{1+2}|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -5 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 2 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-2(1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-5 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{aligned}|-0\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 2\\end{aligned}|+0\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & -5 \\\\ 4 & 2\\end{aligned}|) \\\\  & =-2((-5\\cdot 2-4\\cdot 2)-0+0) \\\\  & =-2\\cdot (-18) \\\\  & =36\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
