    "q-32746": {
      "dom_id": "step-q32746",
      "name": "Question 12",
      "problem": "Calculate the determinant of the matrix\n$W=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 8 & 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}].$",
      "worked_solution": "We use the cofactor expansion along the first row:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(W) & ={w}_{11}{C}_{11}+{w}_{12}{C}_{12}+{w}_{13}{C}_{13}+{w}_{14}{C}_{14} \\\\  & =1\\cdot {C}_{11}+0\\cdot {C}_{12}+5\\cdot {C}_{13}+0\\cdot {C}_{14} \\\\  & ={C}_{11}+5{C}_{13} \\\\  & =1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & ∗ & ∗ & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ ∗ & 3 & 0 & 4 \\\\ ∗ & 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}|+5\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}∗ & ∗ & 5 & ∗ \\\\ 2 & 0 & ∗ & 0 \\\\ -1 & 3 & ∗ & 4 \\\\ 8 & 0 & ∗ & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-1)^{1+1}|\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}|+5\\cdot (-1)^{1+3}|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 8 & 0 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}|+5|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 8 & 0 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}|-0\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}|+0\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|+5(2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}|-0\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-1 & 4 \\\\ 8 & -2\\end{aligned}|+0\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ 8 & 0\\end{aligned}|) \\\\  & =10(3\\cdot (-2)-4\\cdot 0) \\\\  & =10\\cdot (-6) \\\\  & =-60\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
