    "q-131122": {
      "dom_id": "step-q131122",
      "name": "Question 14",
      "problem": "Calculate the determinant of the matrix\n$W=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 3 & 6\\end{aligned}].$",
      "worked_solution": "We use the cofactor expansion along the first row:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(W) & ={w}_{11}{C}_{11}+{w}_{12}{C}_{12}+{w}_{13}{C}_{13}+{w}_{14}{C}_{14} \\\\  & =0\\cdot {C}_{11}+(-1)\\cdot {C}_{12}+0\\cdot {C}_{13}+2\\cdot {C}_{14} \\\\  & =-{C}_{12}+2{C}_{14} \\\\  & =-1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}∗ & -1 & ∗ & ∗ \\\\ 0 & ∗ & 0 & 1 \\\\ 3 & ∗ & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & ∗ & 3 & 6\\end{aligned}|+2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}∗ & ∗ & ∗ & 2 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0 & ∗ \\\\ 3 & 2 & 1 & ∗ \\\\ 0 & 4 & 3 & ∗\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-1\\cdot (-1)^{1+2}|\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 6\\end{aligned}|+2\\cdot (-1)^{4+1}|\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 6\\end{aligned}|-2|\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 6\\end{aligned}|-0\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{aligned}|+1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}|-2(0\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{aligned}|-5\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}|+0\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}|) \\\\  & =9-2\\cdot (-5)\\cdot 9 \\\\  & =9+90 \\\\  & =99\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
