    "q-131099": {
      "dom_id": "step-q131099",
      "name": "Question 15",
      "problem": "Calculate the determinant of the matrix\n$T=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 & -10 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3 & -25\\end{aligned}]$",
      "worked_solution": "We use the cofactor expansion along the first row:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(T) & ={t}_{11}{C}_{11}+{t}_{12}{C}_{12}+{t}_{13}{C}_{13}+{t}_{14}{C}_{14} \\\\  & =0\\cdot {C}_{11}+0\\cdot {C}_{12}+0\\cdot {C}_{13}-10\\cdot {C}_{14} \\\\  & =-10{C}_{14} \\\\  & =-10\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}∗ & ∗ & ∗ & -10 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 & ∗ \\\\ 1 & 3 & 2 & ∗ \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3 & ∗\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-10(-1)^{1+4}|\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =10(0\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}|-4\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}|+0\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|) \\\\  & =10(0-4(1\\cdot 3-1\\cdot 2)+0) \\\\  & =10\\cdot (-4) \\\\  & =-40\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
